{"id":"dell-earnings-q3-fy2027-breakdown","title":"DELL Earnings Q3 FY2027 breakdown","section":"Earnings","date":"2026-11-24","html":"<p>Dell reported after the close on Tuesday, Nov 24, 2026. The stock had fallen 11.8% in the session to $295.28 on HPE's margin warning, then traded about $307.7 (+4.2%) after hours. Numbers come from Dell's 8-K extract, its prepared remarks and the call transcript as reported by Investing.com, the Motley Fool and Stocktwits; consensus figures differ slightly by source.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-numbers-against-expectations\">The numbers against expectations</h3>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Q3 FY27</th><th>Expected / prior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Revenue</td><td>$54.9B (+103% y/y), a record</td><td>about $49.2–49.3B</td></tr><tr><td>Non-GAAP EPS</td><td>$9.45 (+265%)</td><td>about $6.56–6.60</td></tr><tr><td>GAAP EPS</td><td class=\"n\">$8.82</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Infrastructure (ISG) revenue</td><td>$41.97B (+198%); operating margin 17.0%</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>AI-optimized servers</td><td>$22.03B (+291%)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Traditional servers and networking</td><td>$15.01B (+235%)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Storage</td><td>$4.93B (+24%)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>PCs (CSG)</td><td>$12.89B (+3%); margin 5.5%</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>AI orders / backlog</td><td>$60.2B orders; record $132.3B backlog</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Operating cash flow</td><td>$4.46B (+280%)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Q4 revenue guide</td><td>$56.25B midpoint (+69%); EPS $8.40</td><td>above consensus (Stocktwits)</td></tr><tr><td>FY27 revenue guide</td><td>$202B, up from $192B</td><td>about $193.5B</td></tr><tr><td>FY27 EPS guide</td><td>$29.68, up from $25.50</td><td>about $26 (InvestingPro)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"what-management-said-about-the-road-ahead\">What management said about the road ahead</h3>\n<ul><li>&quot;We are now a different company, with Infrastructure Solutions Group (ISG) driving the vast majority of our profit and growth.&quot; (Jeff Clarke)</li><li>&quot;The demand is further ahead of supply in calendar 2027 than it has been in 2026.&quot; (Clarke, on the call)</li><li>&quot;I don't know of a customer that's on the sideline.&quot; (Clarke)</li><li>About $180B of orders in the last four quarters; more than 7,500 AI Factory customers.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-management-is-worried-about\">What management is worried about</h3>\n<ul><li>Margins: the CFO said ISG margins &quot;will sequentially moderate&quot; as the North America mix normalizes, from 17% to just under 15% in Q4 (Stocktwits).</li><li>Components: Clarke sees &quot;nothing that suggests that we're going to see price declines in enterprise, NAND, and DRAM for servers.&quot;</li><li>PCs stay soft next year; consumer PCs fell 15%.</li><li>Inventory has nearly tripled since January to $29.4B; debt $37.7B (Motley Fool).</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"the-big-worry-both-ways\">The big worry, both ways</h3>\n<ul><li>Bull: a $132.3B backlog and demand ahead of supply into 2027 make revenue visible for a year.</li><li>Bear: revenue grows into falling margins. HPE's call the night before (memory scarce into 2H 2028, AI margins down to about 14% from 18.4%) is the same story at a weaker competitor, and Dell's own Q4 margin guide confirms the direction.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"money-plans\">Money plans</h3>\n<ul><li>Record $4.9B returned in the quarter ($4.38B buybacks, $398M dividends); a new $25B buyback authorization; at least 80% of adjusted free cash flow to be returned.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"people-and-governance\">People and governance</h3>\n<ul><li>No leadership changes announced. Sources disagree on Clarke's title (vice chairman and COO in the release; CEO in one transcript label).</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-it-says-about-the-market-and-the-names-it-moves\">What it says about the market, and the names it moves</h3>\n<ul><li>AI infrastructure demand is not the problem; supply and component costs are. That reads across to SMH, NVDA, AMD, VRT, BE and CRDO on the watchlist: the hardware trade is a margin story now.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"the-chart\">The chart</h3>\n<figure class=\"chart\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" data-ticker=\"DELL\" viewBox=\"0 0 760 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"DELL · daily · retracement of Jan 21 $109.55 → Sep 18 $594.69 + 14/30-day chart\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"760\" height=\"420\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" class=\"c-bg\"/><text x=\"8\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#20242C\" class=\"c-ink\">DELL · daily · retracement of Jan 21 $109.55 → Sep 18 $594.69 + 14/30-day</text><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"380.0\" y2=\"380.0\" stroke=\"#E3DACB\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-grid\"/><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"295.0\" y2=\"295.0\" stroke=\"#E3DACB\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-grid\"/><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"210.0\" y2=\"210.0\" stroke=\"#E3DACB\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-grid\"/><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"125.0\" y2=\"125.0\" stroke=\"#E3DACB\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-grid\"/><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"40.0\" y2=\"40.0\" stroke=\"#E3DACB\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-grid\"/><line x1=\"8\" x2=\"610\" y1=\"296.9\" y2=\"296.9\" stroke=\"#2F6E4A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"1 4\" opacity=\"0.7\"/><text x=\"11\" y=\"293.9\" font-size=\"9.5\" fill=\"#2F6E4A\" opacity=\"0.9\">Put wall $300.00 · OI 2,795</text><line x1=\"10.1\" x2=\"10.1\" y1=\"203.6\" y2=\"225.8\" stroke=\"#A63A2E\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-dn\"/><rect x=\"8.8\" y=\"209.6\" width=\"2.6\" height=\"9.5\" fill=\"#A63A2E\" class=\"c-dn\"/><line x1=\"14.4\" x2=\"14.4\" y1=\"209.0\" y2=\"226.4\" stroke=\"#2F6E4A\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-up\"/><rect x=\"13.0\" y=\"213.7\" width=\"2.6\" height=\"1.8\" fill=\"#2F6E4A\" class=\"c-up\"/><line x1=\"18.6\" x2=\"18.6\" y1=\"207.9\" y2=\"250.1\" stroke=\"#A63A2E\" stroke-width=\"1\" class=\"c-dn\"/><rect x=\"17.3\" y=\"211.9\" w