<line x1=\"518.6\" x2=\"610.0\" y1=\"290.5\" y2=\"290.5\" stroke=\"#C9A84C\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"608.0\" y=\"286.5\" font-size=\"10.5\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#7A5E12\">AFTER HOURS $307.71</text></svg></figure>\n<p>DELL's Jan 21 → Sep 18 run ($109.55 → $594.69) has given back 61.8% of itself: that level is $294.87, and Tuesday's low ($290.50) wicked under it while the close ($295.28) held it by 41 cents. The 14-day ($328.05) is under the 30-day ($395.72); the 50-day ($461.78) is still over the 200-day ($349.37). The weekly options priced about ±$39.50 (13.4%) into the report; the after-hours move was about a third of that.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-trade\">The trade</h3>\n<p>No trade. Implied volatility was near 190% on the weekly contracts and every December contract near the money costs well over $800. What to watch: whether $294.87 holds on the closes into Friday; a close back over the 14-day ($328.05) would be the first sign of repair.</p>\n<p>Sources: <a href=\"https://investors.delltechnologies.com/sec-filings/all-sec-filings/content/0001571996-26-000050/0001571996-26-000050.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Dell 8-K</a> · <a href=\"https://investors.delltechnologies.com/_assets/_89e9d1cb2fc1be4c6ed302d35e1514c6/delltechnologies/db/3595/34778/prepared_remarks/Q3_FY27_Prepared_Remarks.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Prepared remarks</a> · <a href=\"https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-dell-tops-q3-2026-estimates-stock-rebounds-after-drop-93CH-5049292\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Investing.com transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/11/24/dell-just-reported-earnings-and-raised-its-forecast-by-usd10-billion-is-the-stock-a-buy-after-tuesday-s-selloff/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Motley Fool</a> · <a href=\"https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/dell-stock-gains-after-hours-as-ai-server-boom-leads-record-q3-prompts-third-annual-forecast-hike